From 7d74b17d2ef743d05edc3e03d0d0d0e99223ad80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 20:52:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] the Dashboard reports the workload instead of the row
 count, and the contrast gate stops lying
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Seven of the eight Gewerke tiles read 1.298. That figure is "projects whose
row for this Gewerk carries a recognised status" — every project has all 14
rows and almost all are filled in, so it is the project count for nearly
every Gewerk, forever. It moves only when data is added. It reads as "1.298
EEA-Prüfungen" and the real number is 814; ITK is 510, GA 158, HFT 100. Six
Gewerke were not shown at all, and the two with no approval anywhere in
their vocabulary — UM and BIM — were among the six.

shared/portfolio-metrics.ts derives the honest figures, and the Dashboard
now agrees with the Gewerk tabs: 814 on the tile, 814 on /bvb-eea. All
fourteen are shown, ranked by a risk score whose weights are printed on the
panel rather than buried in an expression, and labelled a ranking heuristic
because that is what it is. A Gewerk that has approved nothing says so
instead of showing 0% as if it were failure.

PRÄSENTATIONSMODUS is opt-in, and that is a decision. Content that moves
while it is read is hostile at a desk; on a wall display rotation is the
only way to fit fourteen cards in one frame. So: off by default, pauses on
pointer or focus entry — hover alone never fires for a keyboard user — and
never auto-advances under prefers-reduced-motion.

PORTFOLIO-RELIEF is deliberately not a rotating 3D bar chart. Perspective
makes a near bar read larger than an identical far one and the top face
hides where a bar ends, so a reader comparing two columns compares two
projections rather than two numbers. Here depth carries nothing that must
be compared by eye: every cell prints its exact count, position is a fixed
grid, and elevation is a redundant encoding of the same value. "Flach"
shows the identical numbers. CSS 3D rather than WebGL — the bundle already
carries 382 kB of charting and 150 kB of mapping.

DIAGNOSTICS say what they cannot measure. The median open check is 452 days
old and 328 are past a year; 388 more carry no Prüfdatum and are reported
as unageable rather than dropped. Five reviewers hold 46% of open work.
"Prüfung erfolgt" is a real status on 229 rows that belongs to no lifecycle
bucket, so the panel names it and its count — otherwise open + zugestimmt +
blockiert looks complete while missing hundreds of rows. A Projektnummer is
a programme id: 1,298 projects carry 385 numbers, one of them 98 times,
stated as a fact rather than counted as an error.

THE CONTRAST GATE HAD BEEN BLIND. Its colour parser matched rgb()/rgba()
and returned null for everything else — and Tailwind v4 emits oklch() for
its whole palette, so every text-emerald-600, text-amber-600 and
text-blue-600 in the app was silently skipped. The parser now resolves any
CSS colour through a 1×1 canvas, solved against white and black backdrops
because dividing a single painted pixel by its own alpha amplifies
quantisation by 1/a: at bg-primary/5 that turned a barely-tinted white into
solid red and produced channel values above 255.

Un-blinded, it found thirteen real WCAG failures, none of them new:
emerald-600 and amber-600 on white (3.65:1 and 3.20:1), blue-600, rose-600
and red-600 on the dark background with no dark variant, emerald-600
initials on an emerald-100 disc, and — on every primary button in the app —
white text on the hover state, because hover:bg-primary/90 lightens the red
towards the page behind it and takes 4.53:1 down to 4.40:1. Hover now
darkens.

Gates: tsc clean, biome unchanged at 72 pre-existing warnings, 235 unit
tests (17 new), build clean, e2e 72/72 (9 new), stress 8/8, check-ui clean
across 6 routes x 12 scenarios x 3 viewports x 4 theme combinations.
